  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning to the residential block after the morning shift at the mine.
    - Collecting the weekly coal allocation for the eastern apartments.
    - End of shift at Coal Face B. Nothing to report.
    midDaysReasons:
    - The east shaft was sealed this morning. I'm going home.
    - Picking up protective gear from the equipment depot before the next rotation.
    - Double shift at C shaft. I need to sleep.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - The mine is closed. All of them. I'm just going home.
    - Nowhere else to go. The mine is shut.
    - Returning to my bunk. That is all.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Visiting a beach resort that was buried in a rockfall in 1971.
    - Buying flowers at the market that closed when I was thirty.
    - Going to see my brother who moved away before I was born.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Meeting the mine supervisor at an office that no longer exists.
    - I need to start a shift at a shaft that was sealed last Tuesday.
    - Going to the recreation hall that is now a field hospital.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - The mine is running fine. I need to get back underground immediately.
    - Someone is still tapping from below. I need to answer.
    - I heard the foreman call my name. He needs me back down there.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Long shift. Papers are in order.
    - Just off the morning rotation. Coal Face B.
    - I know I'm dirty. The showers at the shaft were out again.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - They moved us to C shaft. Longer walk.
    - Eleven hours today. I don't complain.
    - The ventilation has been bad this week. We manage.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - They closed the mine. I don't know what I'm supposed to do now.
    - Just going home.
    - I used to know what my day was.
