  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0126d7c6e9586af4b99c87708fd95382, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The mine. B shaft. Finished at six.
    midDaysAnswer: C shaft now. Longer walk. Finished at six.
    finalDaysAnswer: Nowhere. The mine is closed. I walked for a while.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Home. I wasn't at the mine today. My back. I stayed
      in and rested.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Home. I haven't been to the mine in several days. My back
      has been bad. Nothing unusual.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The mine! B shaft. Running perfectly. Full crew. Everyone
      is there. No problems at all.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Coal dust. Always coal dust. My lungs are fine. The doctor says
      fine.
    midDaysAnswer: Some dizziness. The ventilation in C shaft has been poor. It happens.
    finalDaysAnswer: I'm tired. More than usual. But I'm always tired.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Nothing. I feel very well. Better than I have in years.
      Very clear-headed.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No dizziness at all. Lungs are clear. I haven't been near
      the mine, so no dust. Everything is fine.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Perfect health. Strong lungs. Clear head. I feel like
      it's my first year on the coal face.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My wife. Two sons. Top floor, east block.
    midDaysAnswer: My wife. The boys left for the west district last month. Just
      the two of us now.
    finalDaysAnswer: My wife. Just us. She doesn't say much either.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Just me. My wife left some time ago. I don't talk about
      it.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: All four of us still. Wife and both boys. East block.
      Nothing has changed.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My wife and both sons. We all eat together every night.
      Every night without fail.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - B shaft today. Long one.
    - I know I smell. The showers at the mine were out again.
    - Papers are in order. Always are.
    midDays:
    - They moved us to C shaft. Longer walk. Worse air.
    - Three men on my crew did not show this morning. Nobody said anything about
      it.
    - I do not complain. I just want to get through.
    finalDays:
    - The mine is closed. First time in thirty years I have had nothing to go back
      to.
    - Just going home. That is all.
    - I used to know what my day was.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
